# The Zig release both archives carry (packed in tos-prepare) and that builds their toolkit (scripts/fetch-zig.sh).
# One line per host: <host> <sha256> <size in bytes> <url>; then `mirror <base url>` lines. The values are the ones in
# https://ziglang.org/download/index.json for this version; `scripts/fetch-zig.sh --check-index` compares them
# with the live index. To move to another Zig: change the lines from index.json, then run the release workflow.
version 0.17.1
x86_64-windows b03f477a1943673e02aca0f570e8030dffd536ce1f45cbc4d3326ec31159562e 100343666 https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.1/zig-x86_64-windows-0.17.1.zip
x86_64-linux 3581863e3cbcfd0fce0efc682ce7e9e93da96668a977791d356a26d2a7e9b17a 57411036 https://ziglang.org/download/0.17.1/zig-x86_64-linux-0.17.1.tar.xz
# Mirrors tried when ziglang.org is slow or down (from https://ziglang.org/download/community-mirrors.txt); the SHA-256 above is what counts.
mirror https://pkg.earth/zig
mirror https://zig.linus.dev/zig
mirror https://pkg.alexrp.com/zig
